    "ls|LS17_S9_U_250": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURAL RESEARCH & EDUCATION \n \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 250 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19th July, 2022 \n \n \nORGANIC VILLAGES \n \n250. SHRI POCHA BRAHMANANDA REDDY: \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE               \nd`f\"k vkSj fdlku dY;k.k ea=h  be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government is promoting organic villages in the country with the \nassistance of Krishi Vigyan Kendra; \n(b) if so, the details of organic villages in the country, State-wise; and \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \n \n THE MINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE      \nd`f\"k vkSj fdlku dY;k.k ea=h       (SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n(a) to (c):  The Krishi Vigyan Kendras  (KVKs) are mandated for technology \nassessment and demonstration for its application and capacity development. KVKs \norganize training for farmers and extension personnel on organic agriculture including \nproduction and use of organic inputs. The KVKs organi zed 4687 such training \nprogrammes with participation of 1.37 lakh farmers and extension personnel during \nlast three years.  \n \nKVKs of Sikkim State are organizing all its activities on organic agriculture as \nthe Sikkim Government has declared it as Organic State. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S9_U_251": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY & DAIRYING \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY & DAIRYING  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 249 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19th JULY, 2022 \n \nONE HEALTH PILOT PROJECT \n249. Shri Prataprao Jadhav:  \nShri Sanjay Sadashivrao Mandlik:  \nShri Shrirang Appa Barne:  \nShri Dhairyasheel Sambhajirao Mane:  \nShri Bidyut Baran Mahato:  \nShri Subrat Pathak:  \nShri Sudheer Gupta:  \nShri Sangam Lal Gupta:  \nShri Manoj Tiwari:  \nShri Ramesh Bidhuri:  \nShri Ravi Kishan:  \nShri Ravindra Kushwaha: \n \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING क ृषि और कक सान क ल्याण मंत्री  \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying (DAHD) has launced/proposes to launch \nOne Health Pilot Project in the country in order to bring stake holders from animal, human and \nenvironment health on one common platform; \n \n(b) if so, the details and the reasons therefor along with the salient features of the said project; \n \n(c) the names of the States in which it is likely to be launched; \n \n(d) whether the Government has earmarked any funds for the above said project and if so, the details \nthereof and the manner in which funds are likely to be released for the project; \n \n(e) the manner in which DAHD is likely to be beneficial to the fishermen in the country; and \n \n(f) the other steps taken by the Government for the economic upliftment and welfare of the fishermen \nin the country? \n \n ANSWER \nTHE HON’BLE MINISTER OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY & DAIRYING \n(SHRI PARSHOTTAM RUPALA)  \n\n  \n(a) to (c ) Yes sir, Department of Animal Husbandry & Dairying (DAHD) has already initiated \nimplementation of  One-Health in the country with technical support of Bill and Melinda Gates \nfoundation (BMGF). )  Two pilot projects were already launched in Uttarakhand on 6th April, 2022 and \nin Karnataka on 28th June, 2022.   \n \nThe salient features of this project includes: \ni. Institutionalizing mechanism for intersector coordination for information sharing  \nii. Capacity building of multisectoral professionals in field and laboratories \niii. Integrating the  network of diagnostic laboratories with special  focus on strengthening \ncommunication  \niv. Developing and Implementing  communication tools and channels  for both field functionaries \nand community with emphasis on animal health related issues \n (d ) The re is no financial invovement from  the Department under this project, which is supported by \nBMGF. \n (e ) to (f) The project does not work towards the economic upliftment and welfare of fisherman in the  \ncountry.  \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S9_U_252": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 252 \nANSWERED ON-19.07.2022 \n \nSVAMITVA SCHEME IN KERALA \n  \n252. DR. M.P. ABDUSSAMAD SAMADANI: \n  \nWill the Minister of PANCHAYATI RAJ be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether Survey of Villages Abadi & Mapping with Improvised Technology in Village \nAreas (SVAMITVA) scheme is being implemented in Kerala; \n \n(b) if so, the details of each project implemented in Kerala with their respective names; and \n \n(c) the details of funds alloca ted to these projects in Kerala during the last three financial \nyears? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PANCHAYATI RAJ  \n(SHRI KAPIL MORESHWAR PATIL) \n \n(a) and (b) The Central Sector Scheme, SVAMITVA, aims to provide the ‘Record of Rights’ to \nvillage household owners possessing houses in inhabited areas (Abadi) with issuance of legal \nownership rights (Property cards/Title deeds). Under the scheme, the land parcels in rural inhabited \narea of all the villages, called Abadi in some States, are surveyed. It is being implemented with the \ncollaborative efforts of the Ministry of Panchayati Raj, Survey of India (SoI), State Revenue \nDepartment, State Panchayati Raj Department and National Informatics Centre. States need to sign \nMemorandum of Understanding (MoU) with  SoI for implementation of the scheme. So far 31 \nStates/UTs, including the States of Kerala, have signed MoU with SoI. As far as the State of Kerala \nin concerned, the MoU was signed between the Survey of India and the State Government of \nKerala on 20th April 2021. So far, the drone flying has been completed in 51 villages of 13 districts \nof Kerala. The details are attached at Annexure. \n \n(c) Under the scheme, funds to Survey of India are provided for two components – Large Scale \nMapping (LSM) using drones an d establishment of Continuous Operating Reference Station \n(CORS). Funds on limited scale are also provided directly to States for Information, Education, \nCommunication (IEC) and setting up of State Project Monitoring Unit (SPMU). The Survey of \nIndia has be en released funds to the tune of Rs. 63.84 lakh for LSM and Rs. 6.72 crore for \nestablishing 28 CORS in Kerala. \n*** \n\nAnnexure \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (a) and (b) of the Lok  Sabha UnStarred Question No. \n252 answered on 19.07.2022 regarding ‘SVAMITVA scheme in Kerala’. \n \nCompletion of Drone Flying under SVAMITVA Scheme in Kerala as on 13.07.2022 \n \nSl no. District Village \n1 \nThiruvananthapuram \nAttingal \n2 Malayinkeezhu \n3 Neyyatingara \n4 Karakkulam \n5 Veiloor \n6 Kallara \n7 Melthonnakkal \n8 Thekkada \n9 \nKollam \nKilikollur \n10 Mangad \n11 Kottankara \n12 Thalavoor \n13 \nPathanamthitta \nOmalur \n14 Kozhenchery \n15 Chenneerkara \n16 Elanthoor \n17 \nKottayam \nNaduvila \n18 Vaikkom \n19 Udayanapuram \n20 Alappuzha Pulimkunnu \n21 \nErnakulam \nPoonithura \n22 Pallarimangalam \n23 Kanayannur \n24 Thiruvankulam \n25 Trissur Chiyyaram \n\n26 Koorkachery \n27 Kanimangalam \n28 Alappad \n29 Vadakkumuri \n30 \nPalakkad \nThiruthala \n31 Thirumittakkodu 1 \n32 Pattithara \n33 \nKannur \nKannur 1 \n34 Kannur 2 \n35 Thalassery \n36 Pallikkunnu \n37 Kottayam \n38 \nMalapuram \nPerumanna \n39 Adavanad \n40 Malapuram \n41 Ananthavoor \n42 \nKozhikode \nThuneri \n43 Thikkodi \n44 Nadapuram \n45 Cheruvanoor \n46 \nKasaragod \nChengala \n47 Bombrana \n48 Kasaragod \n49 \nWayanad \nMananthavadi \n50 Ambalavayal \n51 Valad \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S9_U_253": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.253 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.08.2022 \n \n                                     RAIL VIKAS NIGAM LIMITED  \n                \n *253. SHRI HANUMAN BENIWAL: \n         \n           Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state : \n \n(a)  whether the Rail Vikas  Nigam Ltd (RVNL), a PSU of Ministry of \nRailways, executed the new line construction work for a private \ncompany, Krishnapatnam Railway Company Limited (KRCL) and \nincurred excess expenditure without receiving the requisite \npayment from KRCL;  \n(b) if so, the  details of outstanding amount (including interest) \nreceivable by RVNL from this private company; \n(c) whether this is a case of diversion of railway money to private \ncompany as unsecured advance and if so, the details thereof;  \n(d)  the details of rules an d procedures laid down by the Government \nin this regard; \n(e) whether the same has been followed in this case by the RVNL \nofficials and if so, the details thereof; and  \n(f)  if not, the action taken by the Railways in this regard? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS &  INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n  \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n \n(a) to (f)  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n                                                        **** \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPL Y TO PARTS (a) to ( f) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO.253 BY SHRI HANUMAN BENIWAL TO BE ANSWERED IN \nLOK SABHA ON 03.08.2022 REGARDING  RAIL VIKAS NIGAM LIMITED  \n \n(a) Krishnapatnam Railway Company Limited (KRCL) is one of the Six \nSpecial Purpose Vehicles (SPVs) set up by RVNL for last mile rail \nconnectivity to ports and industrial areas. \nKRCL has entered into a Concession Agreement with Ministry of \nRailways for the rail line and the land belongs to Indian Railways. \nRVNL has constructed the rail connectivity afte r entering into \nConstruction Agreement between RVNL and KRCL. \nThe funding of this rail connectivity Project has been made as per \nfollowing: - \nI) Bank Loans- ₹ 1075 cr. \nII) Equity- ₹ 625 cr. \nIII) Internal Accrual- ₹  89 cr. \nIV) ₹ 838.10 cr. is trade receivable to RVNL (principal amount). \n \n(b) Outstanding principal amount of RVNL is ₹ 838.10 cr. Additionally \nthe interest on this amount as on 31.03.2022 is ₹ 530.18 cr. as per \nAudit Report of Financial Year 2021-22. \n(c) to (f) No railway fund has been spent on this project.  The excess \nexpenditure is made out of Rail Vikas Nigam Limited balance sheet. \nAction as per law being taken against concerned officials.  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S9_U_254": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 254\n \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19\nTH\n \nJULY, 2022\n \n \nREVISION OF RKVY \n \n \n254.\n \nSHRIMATI MANJULATA MANDAL:\n \nSHRI DHANUSH M. KUMAR: \n \n \n \nDR. DNV SENTHILKUMAR. S.:\n \n \n \nSHRI C.N. ANNADURAI: \n \n \n \nDR. PON GAUTHAM SIGAMANI: \n \n \n \nDR. SUBHASH RAMRAO BHAMRE: \n \n \n \nSHRI GAJANAN KIRTIKAR: \n \n \n \nSHRI KANUMURU RAGHU RAMA KRISHNA RAJU: \n \n \n \nSHRI SELVAM G.:\n \n \n \nSHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE: \n \n \n \nSHRI KU\nLDEEP RAI SHARMA: \n \n \n \nDR. AMOL RAMSING KOLHE:\n \n \n \nSHRI SUNIL DATTATRAY TATKARE:   \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nकृ \u0000षएवं\u0000कसानक\u0000याणमं\u0000ी\nbe \npleased to state:\n \n(a) whether the Government has revised Rashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana (RKVY) \nas \nRashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana\n-\nRemunerative Approaches for Agriculture and Allied \nSector Rejuvenation (RKYY\n-\nRAFTAAR) and if so, the details along with the salient \nfeatures thereof;\n \n(b)  whether the RKYY\n-\nRAFTAAR has achieved the objective for which it was\n \nlaunched \nand if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n \n(c)  the details of the projects implemented and the number of beneficiaries covered \nthereunder during the last three years of the current year, State\n-\nwise;\n \n(d)  the funds sanction\ned/spent under the yojana till date, State\n-\nwise; \n \n(e)  the challenges faced by the Government while implementing RKYY\n-\nRAFTAAR;\n \n(f)  whether the Government has reviewed the functioning of RKYY\n-\nRAFTAAR in the \ncountry and if so, the outcome thereof and the co\nrrective measures taken by the \nGovernment for effective implementation of the Yojana; and \n \n(g)  whether this Yojana  will make farming a remunerative economic activity by \nstrengthening farmer’s effort, risk mitigation and promoting agri\n-\nbusiness \nentreprene\nurship, if so, the details thereof?\n \n \n\nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ \u0000षएवं\u0000कसानक\u0000याणमं\u0000ी\n(\nSHRINARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n(a),(b) & (g):\nRashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana (RKVY) has been  revised  with effect from \n01.11.2017  as \nRashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana \n-\n \nRemunerative Approaches for \nAgriculture and Allied Sector Rejuvenation (RKVY\n-\nRAFTAAR) \nwith broad objectives of \nmaking farming a remunerative economic activity through strengthening the farmer’s \neffort, risk mitigation with  \nmore  focus on development and creation of pre & post\n-\nharvest infrastructure, besides promoting agri\n-\nentrepreneurship and innovations.\n \n \n \n1890 \nprojects related to agriculture and allied sectors have been approved by \nvarious States/UTs for implementation und\ner this scheme during the last three  years \nand a total amount of Rs.7240.32\n \ncrore has been released to various State\n/UT\n \nGovernments during this period.\n \nBesides, under Agri\n-\nentrepreneurship programme \nlaunched under the scheme from 2018\n-\n19, 1014 number of s\ntart\n-\nups have been \nsupported with various grass\n-\nroot innovations in agricultural practices that increase \nefficiency and foster innovations.  \n \n \n(c) to \n(e\n):\n  \nRKVY \n-\nRAFTAAR is a combina\ntion of project/infrastructure \nand beneficiary \noriented scheme. Details of beneficiary oriented projects are maintained by the State \nGovernments. State\n-\nwise allocation and release of funds under the scheme during the \nlast three years and current year is given at annexure\n-\nI. Sector\n-\nwise \nprojects approved \nunder the scheme as per the data entered by the concerned State Governments in \nRDMIS portal of RKVY is given at annexure\n-\nII. \n \n \n \nRegarding challenges being faced in implementation of RKVY, reviews are \nconducted from time to time. The schem\ne is being implemented as per operational \nguidelines and also considering various instructions issued by D/o Expenditure   from \ntime to time.  \n \n \n(f):\n \nNITI Aayog has undertaken the evaluation of variousCentrally Sponsored Schemes \nincluding RKVY\n-\nRAFTAAR sche\nme for the period2017\n-\n18 to 2019\n-\n20. The summary of \nthe findings of the evaluation report is given at annexure\n-\nIII.  \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure \n-\n \nI \n \nStatement annexed in reply to the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 254 due for answer on \n19.07.2022\n \n \nState\n-\nwise allocation under RKVY during 2019\n-\n20 to 2022\n-\n23 as on 12.07.2022\n \n(Rs. in crore) \n \nSl. No.\n \nName of the States\n \nAllocation  \n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n2021\n-\n22\n \n2022\n-\n23\n \n1\n \nAndhra Pradesh \n \n210.34\n \n185.01\n \n203.47\n \n183.20\n \n2\n \nArunachal Pradesh\n \n19.46\n \n26.46\n \n14.74\n \n18.66\n \n3\n \nAssam\n \n219.93\n \n188.49\n \n159.95\n \n226.86\n \n4\n \nBihar \n \n184.53\n \n179.16\n \n140.95\n \n131.80\n \n5\n \nChhattisgarh  \n \n132.66\n \n126.44\n \n91.03\n \n80.84\n \n6\n \nGoa\n \n16.28\n \n17.87\n \n17.94\n \n17.80\n \n7\n \nGujarat \n \n118.07\n \n134.17\n \n145.84\n \n130.32\n \n8\n \nHaryana\n \n68.97\n \n86.11\n \n83.89\n \n57.69\n \n9\n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \n24.90\n \n27.02\n \n23.54\n \n22.37\n \n10\n \nJammu & Kashmir \n \n21.17\n \n8.20\n \n10.58\n \n9.00\n \n11\n \nJharkhand \n \n109.50\n \n93.58\n \n60.02\n \n50.57\n \n12\n \nKarnataka \n \n191.20\n \n249.72\n \n218.84\n \n206.09\n \n13\n \nKerala\n \n66.95\n \n63.42\n \n63.11\n \n55.74\n \n14\n \nMadhya Pradesh \n \n182.53\n \n170.96\n \n197.46\n \n180.50\n \n15\n \nMaharashtra\n \n261.76\n \n290.88\n \n249.23\n \n229.77\n \n16\n \nManipur \n \n16.33\n \n19.23\n \n23.25\n \n31.57\n \n17\n \nMeghalaya \n \n20.06\n \n21.35\n \n23.70\n \n31.90\n \n18\n \nMizoram \n \n11.74\n \n13.28\n \n33.65\n \n49.37\n \n19\n \nNagaland\n \n38.83\n \n33.88\n \n17.14\n \n22.64\n \n20\n \nOdisha \n \n207.