    "ls|LS17_S9_U_397": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 397 \nANSWERED ON 19.07.2022 \n \nSETTING UP OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES  \n \n397. SHRI RAJESHBHAI CHUDASAMA:  \nSHRIMATI POONAM MAHAJAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of HEAVY INDUSTRIES भारी उद्योग मंत्री be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether there is any proposal under consideration of the Government for setting up \nany heavy industry in public or private sector with the assistance of World Bank or any other \ninternational organisation particularly in the backward districts of the countr y and if so, the \ndetails thereof, State and location-wise; and  \n \n(b) the funds allocated/proposed to be allocated for this purpose and the time by which the \nwork in this regard is likely to be started? \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR HEAVY INDUSTRIES \n(SHRI KRISHAN PAL GURJAR) \n \n(a): Since Industry is a State Subject, the Ministry of Heavy Industries (MHI) does not \nmaintain any centralized data relating to setting up of heavy industries in public or private \nsector in the country. \n \n(b): Does not arise. \n--------------  \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S9_U_398": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK \nSABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.398\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19\nTH\n \nJULY 2022\n \n \nFEMALE \nFARMERS\n \nIN GUJARAT\n \n \n398. SHRI MOHANBHAI KALYANJIKUNDARIYA:\n \n \nWill \nthe Minister of AGRICULTURE & FARMERS WELFARE\n \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe \npleased to state:\n \n \n(a) the total number of female farmers in the Gujarat,\n \ndistrict\n-\nwise;\n \n(b) whether the Government has provided any\n \ntechnical assistance, training or any other \nkind \nof\n \nassistance to female farmers using the said data;\n \n(c) if so, the details thereof, district\n-\nwise;\n \n(d) if not, whether any such scheme which provides\n \nbenefits to female farmers is under \nconsideration; and\n \n(e) if so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n(a): \nAs per Agriculture Census 2015\n-\n16,d\nistrict\n-\nwis\ne total number\n \nof female operational \nholders\n \nin Gujarat\n \nis given in \nAnnex\n-\nI\n.\n \n \n(b) &\n(\nc\n):\n \nGo\nvernment is implementing a number of beneficiary oriented \nschemes and\n \ntraining\n \nprogrammes for \nthe benefit of \nfemale farmers.\n \nThese schemes\n \ninter\n-\nalia\n \ninclude \nAgricultural \nTechnology Management Agency (ATMA) scheme, \nKrishi Vigyan Kendras (KVKs), \nSub\n-\nMission\n \non Agriculture Mechanization (SMAM),\n \nDeendayal Antyodaya Yojana\n-\nNational Rural \nLivelihoods Mission (DAY\n-\nNRLM)\n \nand \nPradhan Mantri\n \nKisan\n \nSamman\n \nNidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN)\n. \nDistrict\n-\nwise n\number of \nfemale farmers in Gujarat who have benefitted/trained under these \nschemes/programmes are given in \nAnnex\n-\nII\n.\n \n \n(d) &\n \n(e):  Does not arise.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \nA\nnnex\n-\nI\n \nAnnexure referred to in part (a) of Lok Sabha Unstarred\n \nQuestion No. 398 due for reply on \n19.07.2022\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nDistrict wise number of female operational holders in Gujarat as per \nAgriculture Census 2015\n-\n16\n \nSl. \nNo.\n \nDistrict Name\n \nNumber \n(in Actual)\n \n1\n \nAhmedabad\n \n33\n,\n927\n \n2\n \nAmreli\n \n32\n,\n600\n \n3\n \nAnand\n \n50\n,\n848\n \n4\n \nAravalli\n \n14\n,\n144\n \n5\n \nBanaskatha\n \n34\n,\n421\n \n6\n \nBharuch\n \n32\n,\n867\n \n7\n \nBhavnagar\n \n20\n,\n248\n \n8\n \nBotad\n \n8\n,\n744\n \n9\n \nChhotaUdepur\n \n22\n,\n413\n \n10\n \nDahod\n \n11\n,\n660\n \n11\n \nDang\n \n1\n,\n185\n \n12\n \nDevbhumiDwarka\n \n16\n,\n078\n \n13\n \nGandhinagar\n \n21\n,\n658\n \n14\n \nGirSomnath\n \n16\n,\n157\n \n15\n \nJamnagar\n \n25\n,\n167\n \n16\n \nJunagadh\n \n26\n,\n269\n \n17\n \nKheda\n \n38\n,\n035\n \n18\n \nKutch\n \n59\n,\n059\n \n19\n \nMahisagar\n \n51\n,\n845\n \n20\n \nMehsana\n \n11\n,\n162\n \n21\n \nMorbi\n \n23\n,\n772\n \n22\n \nNarmada\n \n10\n,\n023\n \n23\n \nNavsari\n \n26\n,\n158\n \n24\n \nPanchmahal\n \n21\n,\n090\n \n25\n \nPatan\n \n25\n,\n685\n \n26\n \nPorbandar\n \n10\n,\n753\n \n27\n \nRajkot\n \n46\n,\n410\n \n28\n \nSabarkatha\n \n31\n,\n943\n \n29\n \nSurat\n \n30\n,\n987\n \n30\n \nSurendranagar\n \n36\n,\n294\n \n31\n \nTapi\n \n20\n,\n065\n \n32\n \nVadodara\n \n43\n,\n316\n \n33\n \nValsad\n \n22\n,\n346\n \nTotal\n \n8\n,\n77\n,\n329\n \n\n \nAn\nnex\n-\n \nII\n \n \nAnnexure\n \nreferred to in part (b) &(c) of Lok Sabha \nUnstarred\n \nQuestion No.398 due for reply on \n19\n.07.2022\n \nDistrict wise \nnumber \nof female f\narmers\n \nwho have benefitted/trained under ATMA, KVKs, SMAM, \nDAY\n-\nNRLM\n \n& PM\n-\nKISAN in\n \nGujarat State \n(In Actual)\n \nS.No\n \nDistricts\n \nNo. of female beneficiari