    "ls|LS17_S9_U_405": "O.I.H. \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nDEPARTMENT OF FISHERIES \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 405 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19TH JULY, 2022 \nProjects under Centrally Sponsored Schemes \n405.  SHRI OMPRAKASH BHUPALSINH alias PAWAN RAJENIMBALKAR:  \nSHRI ARVIND GANPAT SAWANT:  \nSHRI VINAYAK RAUT: \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING, मत्स्य पालन \nपशुपालन और डेयरी मंत्री be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether the Government has received any proposal regarding setting up of fisheries, \nanimal husbandry and dairy projects under Centrally Sponsored Schemes from States \nincluding Maharashtra;  \n(b)  if so, the details of various schemes being implemented by the Government for the \ndevelopment of fisheries, animal husbandry and dairy sector in the country during the last \nthree years, State-wise, including Maharashtra;  \n(c)  the total number of farmers b enefitted there from, so far, State -wise, including \nMaharashtra;  \n(d)  whether the Government has achieved targets of the growth rate in fisheries, animal \nhusbandry and dairy sector and if not, the reasons therefor; and  \n(e)  the corrective steps taken by the Government to promote sectors like animal husbandry and \nfisheries in the country? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \n(SHRI PARSHOTTAM RUPALA) \n(a) to (c):  The Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying, Government of India has \nbeen implementing the following  schemes across the country  including in the State of \nMaharashtra for development of fisheries, animal husbandry and dairy sector:  \n (i)  Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY),  \n(ii)  Fisheries and Aquaculture Infrastructure Development Fund (FIDF),  \n(iii)  Rashtriya Gokul Mission (RGM),  \n(iv)  National Livestock Mission (NLM),  \n(v)  National Programme for Dairy Development (NPDD),  \n(vi)  Dairy Processing and Infrastructure Development Fund (DIDF),  \n(vii)  Supporting Dairy Cooperatives and Farmer Producer Organizations (FPO)  \n(viii)  Entrepreneurship Development and Employment Generation (EDEG), and  \n(ix)  Livestock Health and Disease Control Programme (LHDCP). \n \n\n \n \n \n \nThe State -wise details of central funds sanctioned  for the projects approved for  \ndevelopment of fisheries, dairy and animal husbandry sectors and number of beneficiaries \nbenefitted under the Centrally Sponsored Schemes  during the last three years are furnished at \nAnnexure-I to Annexure-V. \n(d) and (e): The average annual growth rate of fisheries, animal husbandry and dairy sectors \nwas registered at 8.89%, 7.64% and 6.20% respectively during the period of five years  from \n2016-17 to 2020-21. The  Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying, Government \nof India  through various schemes has been complementing and supplementing  the efforts of the \nState Governments/Union Territories (UTs) for promotion and development of animal husbandry, \ndairy  and fisheries sectors and in achieving the sustained and higher growth in these sectors. The \ncentral funds under various demand driven Central Sectors/ Centrally Sponsored Schemes are \nreleased based on the viable proposals received from the States/UTs. Further, review meetings, \nworkshops, seminars, trainings, awareness/ outreach programs are also conducted regularly at the \nNational and Regional levels to promote the fisheries and animal husbandry sectors in the country \nand also to ensure speedy implementation of the schemes.  \n***** \n\nAnnexure-I \nStatement referred to in reply to part (a) and (b) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred \nQuestion No. 405 due for answer on 19th July, 2022:  \n \nState/UT-wise details of central funds released and beneficiaries covered under the \nCentrally Sponsored Schemes implemented for development of fisheries during last three \nyears (2019-20 to 2021-22)  \n(Rs. in lakhs) \nSl.  \nNo \nState/