tates \nName of the State  S.No. Location  of Gokul Gram \nAndhra Pradesh 1 Cattle Breeding farm, Chadalawada, Prakasam district \nTelanagana 1 PVNR Telangana Veterinary University \nKarnataka 1 Amrithmahal, Subcenter, Lingadahalli, Chikkamagaluru, \nDistrict \nGujarat 1 Dharampur, Dist: Porbandar \nMadhya Pradesh 1 Cattle Breeding Farm, Ratona, Sagar  \nMaharashtra 2 Bull Mother Farm , Tathwade Dist.Pune \nBull Mother Farm , Pohara Dist.Amravati \nPunjab 1 Bir Dosanjh Nabha \nHaryana 1 Hisar  \nHimachal Pradesh 1 Thanakhas District Una \nUttar Pradesh 3 DUVASU Mathura \nArazilines Varanasi \nSimra Viran, Shahjahanpur \nArunachal Pradesh 1 Tezu, Lohit  \nChhattisgarh 1 Institutional Gokul Gram Jhalam, District-Bemetra \nBihar 1 Dumranw, Buxar \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S9_U_407": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 407 \n  ANSWERED ON 19/07/2022 \n \n \nROADS BUILT UNDER PMGSY \n \n407.  SHRI SAPTAGIRI SANKAR ULAKA: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the number of roads built under the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) \nduring the last three years, State-wise; \n(b)  whether the Government has the data regarding the number of roads built under the \nsaid yojana in the aspirational districts such as Rayagada/Koraput in the State of \nOdisha; \n(c)  the details of financial incentives given for best performing States, State-wise; and \n(d)  the details of the parameters for determining the best performing States and the \nranking of Odisha in this regard? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n(a)       The number of roads and length constructed under the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak \nYojana (PMGSY)  during the last three years and the current year, State -wise are given at \nAnnexure-I. \n(b)       As per the available information, a total of 38,165 roa ds of 1,58,050 Km length have \nbeen constructed under PMGSY in Aspirational Districts since inception. The details \nregarding roads constructed under PMGSY in the Rayagada and Koraput Districts of Odisha \nare as under:- \n  \n  \nAspirational Districts \nCompleted \nNo. of Roads Road Length (km) \nKoraput 952 4,271 \nRayagada 620 3,331 \n  \n(c)      The details of financial incentive released to States during the last 5 financial years are \ngiven at Annexure-II.  No financial incentive has been given to the states during financial \nyears 2021-22 and 2022-23. \n  \n(d)     The parameters for determining the best performing States for grant of financial \nincentives under PMGSY in 2020-21 were as under:- \n(i)      Achievement of target length of the year (April-December) \n(ii)     Length constructed under New Technology during the year (April-December) \n\n(iii)   % expenditure vs liability during preceding year under routine Maintenance on \nroads under DLP. \n(iv)    Length renewed post DLP (% cumulative road length renewed post 5 year DLP as \nagainst total road length post DLP) \n(v)     % unsatisfactory ongoing (new) works in the last three years as per NQM \ninspections \n(vi)    % unsatisfactory maintenance works in the last three years on roads under DLP. \n(vii)    Funds spent by the state in  the previous financial year, through any of the \ndepartment, for maintenance and renewal of rural roads, per KM of the road length in \nDRRP. \n(viii)    % difference in physical and financial progress of awarded and pending works \nupto December of the year in which proposal of incentive relates. \n(ix)    % No. of roads on which expenditure on routine maintenance during the \npreceding year is less than 60% v/s number of roads. \nThe rank of Odisha as per the parameters for determining the best performing States for grant \nof financial incentives under PMGSY in 2020-21 was 8th. \n***** \n  \n  \n\n            Annexure-I \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (a) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No 407 due \nfor reply on 19.07.2022 \nDetails of roads(no) and road length constructed under PMGSY during the last three \nyears and the current year \nSr. \nNo. \nState 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 2022-23 \n(as on \n13.07.2022) \nNos \nof \nroad \nLength \n(in km) \nNos \nof \nroad \nLength \n(in km) \nNos \nof \nroad \nLength \n(in km) \nNos of \nroad \nLength \n(in km) \n1 Andaman And \nNicobar \n0 0.00 12 30.62 13 14.11 0 0.69 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 101 300.52 61 530.79 160 1,263.18 48 197.66 \n3 Arunachal \nPradesh \n46 1,731.34 25 1,795.50 152 597.51 20 47.02 \n4 Assam 1,288 3,646.74 786 2,684.17 731 2,164.09 48 55.22 \n5 Bihar 852 718.58 586 2,255.01 472 1,861.97 78 175.91 \n6 Chhattisgarh 430 1,952.38 296 4,689.24 464 3,033.59 208 203.